eproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[1,5,12]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[1,12]},{"id":"machir_1877","name":"Machir","also":"Machirites","summary":"Manasseh’s oldest son (Josh. 17:1), or probably his only son (see 1 Chr. 7:14, 15; comp. Num. 26:29-33; Josh. 13:31). His descendants are referred to under the name of Machirites, being the offspring of Gilead (Num. 26:29).","verses":17,"father":"Manasseh","mother":"Concubine the Aramitess","v":[1]},{"id":"gilead_1317","name":"Gilead","also":"","summary":"Son of Manasseh.","verses":11,"father":"Machir","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"zelophehad_3035","name":"Zelophehad","also":"","summary":"First-born, of the tribe of Manasseh, and of the family of Gilead; died in the wilderness. Having left no sons, his daughters, concerned lest their father’s name should be “done away from among his family,” made an appeal to Moses, who, by divine direction, appointed it as “a statute of judgment” in Israel that daughters should inherit their father’s portion when no sons were left (Num. 27:1-11).","verses":9,"father":"Hepher","mother":"","v":[2,6,10,11]},{"id":"tirzah_2868","name":"Tirzah","also":"","summary":"The youngest of Zelophehad’s five daughters (Num. 26:33; Josh. 17:3).","verses":5,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"hoglah_1548","name":"Hoglah","also":"","summary":"Partridge, one of the daughters of Zelophehad the Gileadite, to whom portions were assigned by Moses (Num. 26:33; 27:1; 36:11).","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"mahlah_1895","name":"Mahlah","also":"","summary":"Disease, one of the five daughters of Zelophehad (Num. 27:1-11) who had their father’s inheritance, the law of inheritance having been altered in their favour.","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"milcah_2083","name":"Milcah","also":"","summary":"Belonged to clans of Menasseh.","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"noah_2211","name":"Noah","also":"","summary":"Rest, (Heb. Noah) the grandson of Methuselah (Gen. 5:25-29), who was for two hundred and fifty years contemporary with Adam, and the son of Lamech, who was about fifty years old at the time of Adam’s death.","verses":4,"father":"Zelophehad","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[13]}],"places":[{"id":"jericho_634","name":"Jericho","kind":"City","lat":31.87005,"lon":35.44388,"summary":"Place of fragrance, a fenced city in the midst of a vast grove of palm trees, in the plain of Jordan, over against the place where that river was crossed by the Israelites (Josh. 3:16).","verses":58,"v":[13]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[13]},{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[13]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1,1,1,7218,4940,4940,4940,1568,1568,1121,4353,4353,1121,4519,4519,4940,4940,4940,4940,3130,3130,7126,4872,5387,5387,5387,7218,7218,7218,7218,1121,1121,1121,3478,1696,1696,1696],[559,3068,3068,3068,6680,113,113,5414,5414,776,776,5159,5159,5159,1121,1121,1121,1486,1486